@* The entry of a row of a list, its name or its label, with its detail in small under it (visuel/listes/principes-communs.md,
   Ligne). In a list of the administration, it is no link (visuel/listes/principes-communs.md, Entrée en texte simple): the main
   action alone opens the record, the menu alone the editions and intents of the album an intent targets, a second way to the
   same place being one too many. In a list of the consultation, which has no action, the entry is the link to the record, which
   the list puts in it. The column of the entry is a column of a card: a missing detail is not shown,
   neither a dash nor a mention, nor an empty line (visuel/charte-graphique/convivialite-et-efficacite.md), which every list
   gets from here. *@
<span class="row-entry">@ChildContent</span>
@if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Detail))
{
    <span class="row-entry-detail">@Detail</span>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>The name or the label of the record.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public RenderFragment ChildContent { get; set; } = null!;

    /// <summary>What tells the record apart under its name (its authors, its collections, its album…), if anything does.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Detail { get; set; }
}
